# What the harness compared: the shipped GainKernelRGBA16FHalf4, compiled through
# test/shim (Kernel.cu up to the launcher namespace), against a reference that
# does the same float multiply and the same single round-to-nearest-even
# conversion. Bit equality, not a tolerance: both operands are halves, so the
# product is exact in float and one rounding is all either side applies.
#
# The pitch column is the fixture allocation pitch (bounds + 2 columns, plus the
# pad), not the frame row stride, exactly as the RGBA32F harness allocates.
#
# Not measured, and deliberately so: anything about a GPU. The 16F kernel has no
# launcher (nothing advertises RGBA16F), so there is no device path to time; the
# only claim the bytes support is arithmetic - 8 bytes per pixel against 16 for
# RGBA32F, i.e. half the traffic for the same frame [A]. A device number for
# this kernel is [U].
